This year, the Michael Jackson biopic crossed $1 billion at the global box office. And somewhere inside it, buried in a single scene that lasts barely longer than a blink, there is something the Jackson estate quietly fought to keep out of the final cut. According to 2 separate sources who worked on the production, the director slipped it past them anyway. If you have already seen the film, the odds are extremely high that you walked right past it without realizing what you were looking at. That 2-second moment is the public exposure of a classified neurological protocol that a small group of researchers across 4 continents have spent the last decade documenting inside their own laboratories, and that the $45 billion global wellness industry has spent that exact same decade making absolutely certain you would never encounter in any product they sell you.


The scene takes place in the spring of 1982. A 23-year-old Michael walks into the master bathroom of his Encino estate, picks up a black permanent marker and writes 2 words directly across the glass. 2 words that would become the entire foundation of what insiders working privately with his estate refer to as Jackson''s Method. The film shows you the mirror. It even pans briefly across the bedroom to reveal the affirmations he had taped across the ceiling above his bed.


