When I recited that prayer, I didn''t have to wait a week. It happened immediately. I felt a powerful presence filling my room. It was a peace, a serenity that surrounded my entire body like an embrace from God. In less than 7 days, I was getting out of bed in the morning without that weight.


The pain disappeared, and I started smiling again with a joy I hadn''t felt in years. And the third person was Anna, a writer friend, a talented woman who seemed to carry a cloud of bad luck over her. Everything life gave her was slammed doors and rejection letters. My name is Anna. I''m a writer.


I''ve been writing since I was young, and people always told me I had talent. But it felt like I carried a cloud of bad luck over me. Everything life gave me was a slammed door and a rejection letter, one after another. Then I got the divine code. Exactly 11 days later, my phone rang.


It was a major publishing company, the same one that had ignored me before, and they offered me a huge contract. Over the following months, I sold thousands of copies of my book, and today my life is completely different. I don''t have to worry about money anymore, and I make a living doing what I always dreamed of doing. I didn''t ask anyone to keep it a secret, and I admit I had no idea what was going to happen next. Carlos told his brother, Patricia took it to a friend from church, Ana sent it to her writer''s group, and within a few weeks those 20 words were no longer mine.


They began passing from hand to hand, house to house, city to city, people copying them onto pieces of paper, sending pictures through messages. Reading them out loud to elderly mothers who could no longer read on their own. There were thousands of people, thousands, and my phone would not stop. Messages from people I had never seen in my life, all telling me the same thing. A single mother who had the car at her door ready to take away her belongings because she was about to be evicted, and 3 days later she received a work-from-home job offer.


A 62-year-old man who had already given up on dreaming and went back to working with what he loved. A couple who had already signed their divorce papers and tore them up. People who had absolutely nothing in common. Different ages, different cities, completely different problems. But the result was always the same.


And that''s when I realized it. There wasn''t a single person who opened their heart, recited those 20 words, and came back to tell me that nothing had happened. Not one. That was the moment my legs started shaking. I put the pieces together.


